  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU4Moldova:Start-up city Cahul</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The overall objective of the Action is to support inclusive economic development in Moldova by increasing the potential of the digital economy and enhancing regional competitiveness and its business and investment environment. The specific objective is threefold: 1.Foster partnerships for innovation and entrepreneurship between the private sector, public sector and educational institutions in the region of Cahul. 2.Promote Technology, problem solving and creative solutions in learning and make science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) topics more attractive, for women and men, girls and boys. 3.Facilitate the emergence of start-ups in innovative sectors, build their capacity and investment readiness. The expected results are the establishment of Regional Innovation and Technology Centre in Cahul (EU4Innovation Centre) which will be fully functional and operated. More young people, especially girls and women, will be attracted to start a career/work in the ICT sector through content development in line with the EU4Digital Agenda; expansion of the STEM programmes nationwide and the provision of new up-to-date training courses and implementation of other skills development programmes that meet the needs of the industry. Enabling conditions for innovative sectors start-ups will emerge and grow are will be put in place through strengthening of ICT entrepreneurship culture and community, and the creation of accelerations facilities and programmes for technology start-ups. &lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
